  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Estrone sulfate and Nuclear receptor coactivator 2, mediated through the Androgen receptor. Estrone sulfate is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 1-Deacetoxy-1-oxocaesalmin, Selaginellic acid, and [(2R,3S)-6-oxo-2-[(2S,3S)-3-phenyloxiran-2-yl]-2,3-dihydropyran-3-yl] acetate, all of which are implicated in targeting the Androgen receptor. These compounds, in turn, are linked to the Nuclear receptor coactivator 2, indicating a possible pathway where Estrone sulfate influences the Androgen receptor's activity, which then modulates Nuclear receptor coactivator 2. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.6648) suggest a strong, reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further research is needed to clarify the precise role of Estrone sulfate in this pathway.",
